cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use scspill, please cite it as below."
title: "Synthetic Control Models with Spillovers in Python"
abstract: "scspill is a Python package of synthetic control models that relax SUTVA: estimators that let a treatment reach the donor pool, recovering both the effect on the treated unit and the spillover effect received by every control unit. It currently implements one model, the Bayesian spatial-autoregressive method of Sakaguchi and Tagawa (method='sar'), which routes spillovers through user-supplied spatial weights scaled by a single estimated intensity and returns full posterior uncertainty for both estimands. Further spillover-aware models are planned behind the same interface."
type: software
